From: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: fall back to zlib when zlib-ng.pc is absent

zmbv's CMakeLists hard-requires the zlib-ng pkg-config module, but
distributions (Buildroot among them) commonly build zlib-ng in
ZLIB_COMPAT mode, where it takes over as *the* zlib provider and installs
zlib.pc -- never zlib-ng.pc. Configure then dies with

    No package 'zlib-ng' found

even though zlib-ng is exactly what is installed.

The meson build already handles this, picking the system zlib-ng when it
declares itself and plain zlib otherwise:

    zlib_or_ng_dep = system_zlib_ng_dep.found() ? system_zlib_ng_dep : zlib_dep

Mirror that in CMake. The compat headers/ABI are drop-in, and zmbv.cpp
uses only the classic zlib API, so nothing else needs to change.

Signed-off-by: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>
---
diff --git a/src/libs/zmbv/CMakeLists.txt b/src/libs/zmbv/CMakeLists.txt
index f3fce37..743fcfa 100644
--- a/src/libs/zmbv/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/libs/zmbv/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,6 +1,11 @@
 add_library(zmbv STATIC zmbv.cpp)
 
-pkg_check_modules(ZLIB_NG REQUIRED IMPORTED_TARGET zlib-ng)
+# zlib-ng in ZLIB_COMPAT mode installs zlib.pc and no zlib-ng.pc, so probe
+# for the native name first and fall back to zlib, as the meson build does.
+pkg_check_modules(ZLIB_NG IMPORTED_TARGET zlib-ng)
+if(NOT ZLIB_NG_FOUND)
+  pkg_check_modules(ZLIB_NG REQUIRED IMPORTED_TARGET zlib)
+endif()
 
 target_include_directories(zmbv PUBLIC ..)
 target_link_libraries(zmbv PRIVATE PkgConfig::ZLIB_NG)
